  "description": {
    "short": "Swipe to smash, curve and lob your way past seaside animal rivals in breezy rooftop tennis.",
    "long": "Lobwhistle is rooftop tennis at a sunny seaside resort. Your fox runs to the ball on its own. You only swipe: direction aims the shot, length sets how deep and how hard it flies, and a curve in the swipe puts spin on the ball so it bends and kicks. Glowing tiles on the far court fill a Fever meter. Fill it and your next swipe is a Whistle Shot, a faster spiralling trick shot. Five courts change the bounce: Promenade plays true, Clay Terrace sits up and slows down, Frost Pier skids, the Boardwalk springs, and Whistle Point adds a cross-wind you can read on the windsock. Each animal rival has a signature serve. Win the game, string a long rally, and land tiles in a row to earn three stars. Each day Seaspray Serve, the Lighthouse Open, deals the same seeded three-rival ladder to every player, and your best score is kept on this device. Portrait and landscape both play with one finger, a mouse drag, or the keyboard.",
    "controls": "Swipe to hit: direction aims, length sets power and depth, curve adds spin. A short tap is a safe shot. Desktop: drag with the mouse, or arrows to pick a lane and hold Space to charge. Esc pauses. M mutes.",
    "faq": [
      {
        "q": "How do I get a Whistle Shot?",
        "a": "Land the ball on the glowing tiles. The coral meter fills in six steps, and the next swipe is the trick shot."
      },
      {
        "q": "Why did my shot go long?",
        "a": "A very long swipe is too hard. Ease off so the ball lands inside the far baseline."
      }
    ]
  },
